# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context excludes.
#
# The build context is the REPO ROOT for the backend image
# (`docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .`), so this file governs that build —
# and any other build that also uses the repo root as its context.
#
# This is deliberately a DENY list rather than an allow list. Three things that
# look like build-time-only noise are in fact shipped and load-bearing:
#     db/                    the migrations run from the backend image
#     backend/data/mock/     the seed fixtures the engine reads at startup
#     backend/scripts/       seed_demo.py / precompute.py run as one-off jobs
# An allow list is one forgotten line away from an image that builds fine and
# then cannot migrate its own database, so the safe default here is "included".
#
# NOTE: frontend/ SOURCE is intentionally not excluded, only its installed and
# generated directories. The frontend image may build from this same root
# context; excluding its source would break that build for no gain, since the
# backend Dockerfile COPYs named directories and never the whole context.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Version control and CI ------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Secrets: these must never even enter the build context -----------------
# A file in the context can be read by any COPY, including a careless future
# `COPY . .`, and lands in an image layer that `docker history` will hand to
# anyone who can pull the image. Keep them out at the door.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- Python: virtualenvs, bytecode, tool caches -----------------------------
# .venv is ~128 MB of the wrong platform's binaries (this repo is developed on
# arm64, the image is linux/amd64) and would be actively harmful if copied.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
htmlcov
.tox

# --- Backend: what the running service does not need ------------------------
backend/tests
backend/conftest.py
backend/data/scratch
backend/data/store

# --- Node / Next.js installed + generated output ----------------------------
**/node_modules
frontend/.next
frontend/out
frontend/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# --- Docs and generated documents -------------------------------------------
docs
*.md
*.docx
*.pdf

# --- Local tooling / editor / OS scratch ------------------------------------
.claude
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
Makefile
tasks.py
scripts

# --- Deployment descriptors for other platforms ------------------------------
# Superseded by the Azure Container Apps deployment; no reason to ship it.
render.yaml

# --- Container build files themselves ---------------------------------------
**/Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile.*
.dockerignore
**/docker-compose*.yml

# Not part of the backend image (which copies only backend/ and db/). The
# frontend builds from its own context and frontend/.dockerignore.
infra
loadtest
frontend
*.bundle
